{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Like the overthrowing — all its land.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): the word ארצה refers back to what he mentioned concerning the plagues of the land, for he mentioned that land in general terms, and now he says גפרית ומלח שרפה כל ארצה — 'brimstone and salt, a burning of all its land,' that is, all the land of that land. Or one may say כל ארצה — 'all its land' — meaning all the choicest part of that land, it shall be like the overthrow of Sodom and Gomorrah." "<b>And it is plausible</b> that it alludes to the word כל, and he says כל ארצה — 'all its land' — the land of all, for in the time of goodwill nothing shall be lacking in it, and in the time of wrath, with the withdrawal of the Shekhinah, it shall return: ארצה שרפה — 'its land a burning.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:57.482705794Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}